WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Why does food taste so dull when you have a cold?

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.320
A few covered cups and a pinched nose let your child find out for themselves.

3
00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:14.543
This takes about thirty minutes, with kitchen foods.

4
00:00:15.823 --> 00:00:21.023
Your child practices describing smells in words, matching by smell alone, and

5
00:00:21.023 --> 00:00:22.023
checking a prediction.

6
00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:25.983
They find out how much of flavor comes from the nose.

7
00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.607
Stay with your child throughout.

8
00:00:30.007 --> 00:00:31.267
Use kitchen foods only.

9
00:00:32.627 --> 00:00:36.027
Skip essential oils, perfume, cleaners, and unknown liquids.

10
00:00:37.347 --> 00:00:39.847
Check food allergies before choosing ingredients.

11
00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.567
Skip nuts and nut products.

12
00:00:43.847 --> 00:00:47.327
Use latex-free bands if anyone has a latex allergy.

13
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:51.577
Put a cotton ball in each paper cup you cannot see through.

14
00:00:52.797 --> 00:00:54.517
Add one kitchen smell to each pair.

15
00:00:55.777 --> 00:01:00.137
Try orange peel, coffee, a cinnamon stick, vanilla, or a crushed mint leaf.

16
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.110
You cover each cup with foil and a rubber band.

17
00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.730
Poke four or five holes with a pencil, with the cup on the table.

18
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.630
Label the cups with letters and keep a secret key.

19
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:15.593
Show your child how to waft.

20
00:01:16.733 --> 00:01:18.813
Hold a cup a hand’s width below the nose.

21
00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.313
Wave the air toward your face and sniff gently.

22
00:01:23.673 --> 00:01:25.173
Ask, 'Is it strong or faint?

23
00:01:26.773 --> 00:01:29.353
Pleasant or not?' Mix up the cups and find the pairs.

24
00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:34.207
Next, guess what each smell is, then peel back the foil to check.

25
00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:38.927
It is common to know a smell well and still not find its name.

26
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:42.067
Ask, 'Where have you smelled this before?'

27
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:45.207
Make two covered vanilla cups.

28
00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:49.487
Add one drop to one cotton ball and six to the other.

29
00:01:50.747 --> 00:01:53.627
You handle the extract because it contains alcohol.

30
00:01:55.207 --> 00:01:56.547
Close it and put it out of reach.

31
00:01:58.127 --> 00:02:00.407
Compare the smells, resting a minute between rounds.

32
00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:03.710
Use the smell cups only for smelling.

33
00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:07.450
Wash hands after handling the ingredients.

34
00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.070
Skip tasting if your child has trouble swallowing.

35
00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.650
Have them sit, take small sips, and swallow before talking.

36
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.980
Pour two juices that look alike, such as apple and white grape, into separate small

37
00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:24.720
cups. Mark them one and two.

38
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.900
Then have your child close their eyes and pinch their nose.

39
00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.373
Before your child sips, make a prediction.

40
00:02:33.713 --> 00:02:37.273
With their nose pinched, will they be able to tell which juice it is?

41
00:02:42.767 --> 00:02:44.107
Offer a small sip.

42
00:02:45.507 --> 00:02:47.747
Have your child signal their guess with their fingers.

43
00:02:49.147 --> 00:02:51.047
Then they let go of their nose and swallow.

44
00:02:52.447 --> 00:02:54.227
Ask, 'What changed when you let go?'

45
00:02:54.747 --> 00:02:56.847
Offer water, then repeat with the other juice.

46
00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.590
As you breathe out after a sip, aromas can travel from the back of your mouth to

47
00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.150
your nose. Your brain combines smell and taste.

48
00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.970
Pinching your nose makes much of the flavor fade.

49
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:16.190
Keep cotton balls, rubber bands, and other small pieces away from children under

50
00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:21.830
four. Call nine one one if a child is choking and cannot cough, cry, or talk.

51
00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:24.940
Why does food taste dull with a cold?

52
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:29.000
A stuffy nose makes it harder to smell the food.

53
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:32.840
Compare what your child noticed with what you predicted.
